{"id":"000VTP","title":"Dome 43 - Not the Greatest Fog","author":"psams","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T18:05:00+00:00","posted":"Heute, 12:41 Uhr","rules":"Story\n\nThose networking nanobots continue to evolve and learn, this time regurgitating ideas into new digital forms in the Dome 43 Palin power plant. Will they advance from collective action to emergent intelligence to true consciousness? We can’t have that. This war against idea cloning must be won, our power supply uninterrupted, and this time we are playing by their rules.\n\nInspiration / Nanobot Training\n\n• \"The Greatest Fog\" by Dorlir\n\n• \"Killer Sudoku #4\" by Phistomefel 20 April 2020\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply. Place the digits 1-9 once each in each row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\nDigital Digits: Each digital digit has a visible value, an associated segment count, and the difference or delta between the two. The digits 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 0 have segment counts 2, 5, 5, 4, 5, 6, 3, 7, 6, 6 and thus deltas +1, +3, +2, 0, 0, 0, -4, -1, -3, +6 respectively.\n\nPower Lines: On each orange line with a white stripe, the sum of the values must equal the sum of the segments of the digits on that line. In other words, the sum of the deltas must be zero.\n\nBattery Cages: Digits in orange cages must not be repeated and the segment counts sum to the cage total in the top left corner (if provided).\n\nUnique but equal: In this puzzle, no two battery cages of the same number of cells can contain exactly the same combination of digits, but all must contain an equal sum of segments.\n\nResistors: Cells diagonally or orthogonally joined by an orange dot must have a segment count difference of one, or the number in the dot, if any.\n\nPlay in SudokuPad\n\nThis puzzle employs dynamic fog. Entering a correct digit will clear at least the cell it occupies, and sometimes other cells as well.\n\nDesign Notes - in case you create your own digital digits puzzle.\n\nThe digital digit aide memoire image is 0015ZO. The orange color is #ffad66. The power lines are standard 15 width with a width 5 white line overlay. The resistor dot size is radius 17.\n\nPuzzle Series : The Domes of Planet Palin\n\n• \"Dome 19\" ... nanobots ate the life support control wiring!\n\n• \"Dome 11 - Almost Balanced Products\" ... return of the nanobots\n\n• \"Dome 49 - Triangulation Enumeration Maximization\" ... nano phantom bots\n\n• \"Dome 43 - Not the Greatest Fog\" … the idea cloning nanobot wars\n\n• \"Dome ?? - The Fifth Puzzle in the Series\" ... coming soon to a Raetselportal near you","solutionCode":"Column 9 followed by the number of segments in Box 5.","tags":["Sudoku","Digital (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/repwjvm9tx","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/repwjvm9tx","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T18:05:00+00:00"}